# Differential cases of _match_impl, jq 1.8.2's f_match (src/builtin.c) on joni: one case per construct of
# Oniguruma's syntax list (doc/RE of Oniguruma 6.9, by its section numbers), one per modifier, the match loop's
# steps after an empty match and its offsets in code points, the type errors, and one case per compile-error text
# Oniguruma gives for a pattern. Each case reads its subject, pattern and modifiers from the document on stdin and
# prints every match, or the error, so a difference shows the construct. The prelude-* cases run the functions jq's
# prelude defines over the native, and the order of the native's arguments. A case where joni differs on purpose names
# its DEVIATIONS.md row ("Regex dialect") with deviation and gives the engine's output. Format:
# oracle/src/main/java/dev/rail8/jq/oracle/diff/DiffCase.java. Expected outputs live in regex.rec, written by
# scripts/oracle-record.sh only. Ids are immutable. Every case uses -c.


case regex/escape
arg -c
filter .re as $re | .f as $f | .s | try [match($re; $f)] catch .
stdin {"s": "a.b axb", "re": "a\\\\.b", "f": "g"}\n
end

case regex/alternation
arg -c
filter .re as $re | .f as $f | .s | try [match($re; $f)] catch .
stdin {"s": "cat dog cow", "re": "cat|cow", "f": "g"}\n
end

